---
import CommercialPillars from '../components/CommercialPillars.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
---
<Layout title="Government file protection"><PageHero eyebrow="FOR GOVERNMENT" title="Mission data deserves its own line of defense." text="Protect the path from stored fragments to readable mission data. Cyber Reliant separates storage access from the cryptographic material and processes required for reconstruction." number="03"><a class="button button-dark" href="/request-demo?interest=Government">Request a briefing <Arrow/></a></PageHero>
<CommercialPillars audience="government"/>
<section class="container section split-content"><div><span class="eyebrow">PROTECTION CLOSE TO THE INFORMATION</span><h2>Start with the data.<br/>Respect the mission.</h2></div><div><p class="large-copy">Storage access is not file access.</p><p>Cyber Reliant fragments sensitive files, encrypts the fragments and distributes them across storage locations. Readable reconstruction requires the authorized access path and protected cryptographic material.</p><p>The upcoming network architecture also fragments cryptographic material itself and protects multiple key components through the HSM architecture, separately from distributed file fragments.</p><a class="text-link" href="/technology">Examine the architecture <Arrow/></a></div></section>
<section class="dark-section"><div class="section container"><span class="eyebrow">BUILT AROUND THE MISSION</span><h2>Protection in operational context.</h2><div class="use-case-grid"><article><span class="card-number">01 / MISSION FIT</span><h3>Define the environment.</h3><p>Align protection with classified and sensitive information requirements, contested or disconnected operating conditions, approved applications and storage boundaries.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">02 / TECHNICAL ASSURANCE</span><h3>Examine the implementation.</h3><p>Explore cryptographic protection, the key lifecycle and controlled reconstruction in the context of your mission.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">03 / ACQUISITION</span><h3>Plan the deployment.</h3><p>Discuss deployment options, support and procurement requirements with the product team.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section container split-content"><div><span class="eyebrow">A CLEAR BASIS FOR DISCUSSION</span><h2>Your requirements<br/>set the standard.</h2></div><div class="assurance-note"><h3>Map assurance to your deployment.</h3><p>Bring the requirements for your product version, environment and mission. Examine quantum migration risk, the reconstruction path and opportunities to preserve existing infrastructure. Build a technical briefing around your operational priorities.</p><a class="text-link" href="/request-demo?interest=Government">Request a briefing <Arrow/></a></div></section><CTA government title="Put your mission requirements on the table." text="Explore Zero Trust, quantum readiness and deployment fit with your technical team."/></Layout>
